      "description": "Areas of fog, dense in places with visibility below 100 metres at times, will slowly begin to thin, lift and clear later this morning or, in some spots, not until this afternoon.\n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings",
      "event": "Yellow fog warning",
      "expires": "2026-10-31T10:00:00+00:00",
      "headline": "Fog likely to lead to some transport delays this morning",
      "instruction": "Give yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, leaving extra journey time, or amending plans if necessary. Make sure you know how to switch on your fog lights, and check they are working before setting off on your journey. Bus and train services, as well as flights and ferry travel may also be affected; check for updates from your travel company and follow their advice.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.",
